(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-forging-decision :authorize-press-operation :proceed-with-forging-operation :override-forge-shop-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007131-cloud-itonami-isco-7131-painters-and-related-workers-coverage" "2799007127-cloud-itonami-isco-7127-ac-refrigeration-mechanics-coverage" "2799007124-cloud-itonami-isco-7124-insulation-workers-coverage" "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the forging operation" "proceed with the press operation" "finalize the forging decision" "authorize the press operation" "finalize the press stroke decision" "override the forge-shop safety officer's judgment" "override the forge shop safety officer's judgment" "override forge-shop safety officer judgment" "override forge shop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007221), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/forge-shop-scheduling-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :worker-verified :forge-shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7221"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007221: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7221 Blacksmiths, Hammersmiths and Forging Press Workers forge-shop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7221\n-- Blacksmiths, Hammersmiths and Forging Press Workers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7221\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7221\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Blacksmiths, Hammersmiths and\nForging Press Workers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior\nto this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7221` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7221` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nBlacksmiths and Forging Press Workers work with heated metal and press\nequipment -- real physical-safety stakes (heat exposure, press-crush\nhazard, hot-metal handling). The controlling constraint for this\nvertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a forging-execution decision (e.g. deciding to\nproceed with a specific hammer-strike or press-stroke), or overrides a\nforge-shop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be\na hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-\neligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to FORGE-SHOP SCHEDULING/\nLOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs forging work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, closest domain shape in\nthis wave -- same physical-safety-domain scaffold) -- cloned and read\nin full in this session, independently re-verified working (`clojure\n-M:test` green on a fresh clone before mirroring).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7221` as an OSS forge-shop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for blacksmiths, hammersmiths\nand forging press workers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Forge Worker Advisor ⊣ ForgeWorkerGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **forge-shop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct forging-execution authority** -- it\nmust NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a forging-execution decision (e.g. a specific hammer-strike\nor press-stroke), or any override of a forge-shop safety officer's\njudgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation -- they are\nstructurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/furnace-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a heat-exposure/press-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- forging-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nforging-execution decision or a forge-shop-safety-officer-override.\nThese are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-forging-decision` cannot even be proposed by the reference\nmock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one\nof the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names four concretely-forbidden ops\n(`forgeworker.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-forging-decision`, `:authorize-press-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-forging-operation`,\n`:override-forge-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth,\nand is verified by dedicated unit tests\n(`forgeworker.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-forging-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-press-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-forging-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-forge-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Forge shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered forge shop (`:no-shop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/forge-shop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the four\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a forging\n   or press operation, or overriding a forge-shop safety officer's\n   judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks forging-execution/safety-override language\n   wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a heat-exposure/press-\n  hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about forge-shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  forging-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a forging-\n  execution or safety-officer-override attempt, which is why it is\n  handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural\n  absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"forging\", \"press\", \"hammer\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a forge-shop coordination\nactor working adjacent to forging/press work necessarily discusses\nthose concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `forgeworker.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed\nwith the forging operation\", \"authorize the press operation\",\n\"override the forge-shop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the\ntask's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`forgeworker.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nfurnace-heating task ...\", \"... routed for forge-shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`forgeworker.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand\n`forgeworker.actor-test/holds-a-press-operation-authorization-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7221\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7221` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7221`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 48 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-forging-decision` or\n  `:approve-press-stroke` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize a forging-execution decision exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe (heat exposure, press-crush injury, hot-metal handling),\n  the capability itself must not exist. The only op related to\n  forge-shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human/forge-shop-safety-officer attention and\n  never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a forging-execution\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold forging-materials\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the forging-execution/safety-officer-\n  override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"forging\" \"press\"\n  \"hammer\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  forging/press/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging\n  job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale\n  text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `forge shop` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered worker AND\n  independently-registered forge shop) matches the CRITICAL invariant\n  that a \"worker/forge-shop record must be independently verified/\n  registered before any action\" and the established pattern from\n  prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance\n  checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND\n   forge shop (`:no-worker`/`:no-shop`). Not a forging-execution or\n   safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/furnace-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a forging-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific hammer-strike or press-stroke -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a heat-exposure/press-crush/\n   equipment-condition concern to a human/forge-shop safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the forge-shop\n   safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- forging-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a forging-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na forging-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nhammer-strike or press-stroke) or a forge-shop-safety-officer-\njudgment override -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`forgeworker.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) four concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`forgeworker.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`forgeworker.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-forging-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-press-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-forging-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-forge-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`forgeworker.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a forging operation or override a\nforge-shop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted\nop\n(`forgeworker.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-forge-shop-safety-officer`).\n\nThis actor coordinates FORGE-SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it does\nnot itself perform blacksmithing, hammersmithing or forging-press\nwork, and no combination of confidence, escalation approval or store\nstate can route a forging-execution decision or a forge-shop-safety-\nofficer-judgment override through it.\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 48, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Forge Shop Scheduling Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :forge-shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7221"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7221"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7221)), (:test/simulator :forgeworker.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7221 — Blacksmiths, Hammersmiths and Forging Press Workers Forge-Shop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7221)))
